Algorithm:

1. Start.
2. Input N and N elements.
3. Input the value of K.
4. For each element, count the number of elements smaller than it.
5. If the count is equal to K - 1, then that element is the K-th smallest element.
6. Display the K-th smallest element.
7. Stop.

Complexity Analysis:

Time Complexity:
The program uses two nested loops.
The outer loop runs N times, and for every element, the inner loop also runs N times to count the number of smaller elements.
Therefore,

Time Complexity = N × N
                 = O(N²)

Best Case = O(N²)
Average Case = O(N²)
Worst Case = O(N²)

The same number of comparisons are performed regardless of the arrangement of elements.
